  "Allah says\n\u201cIf you avoid the major sins which you are forbidden.\nWe will remove from your lesser sins and admit you to a noble entrance into paradise\u201d\nMajor Sins:\n51 - Breaking fast intentionally in Ramadan \u2013 Without a valid excuse, it\u2019s a great sin.\n52 - Harming neighbors \u2013 Mistreating neighbors is condemned.\n53 - Using abusive speech \u2013 Insulting others is not part of Islamic character.\n54 - Oppressing weak and helpless people \u2013 Exploiting the vulnerable is haram.\n55 - Dying without repenting from sins \u2013 Delaying repentance leads to regret.\n56 - Arguing excessively and being quarrelsome \u2013 Constant disputes lead to sin.\n57 - Neglecting Friday prayers without excuse \u2013 Skipping Jummah regularly is sinful.\n58 - Cheating in business \u2013 Deception in trade is forbidden.\n59 - Delaying debt repayment without reason \u2013 Unjust delays cause injustice.\n60 - Disobeying Allah\u2019s commands intentionally \u2013 Rejecting religious obligations is a sin.": "2026-10-04T05:38:53.294015",
