  "Allah says\n\u201cIf you avoid the major sins which you are forbidden.\nWe will remove from your lesser sins and admit you to a noble entrance into paradise\u201d\nMajor Sins:\n41 - Rebelling & calling others disbelievers unjustly \u2013 Wrongful accusations lead to destruction.\n42 - Spying and eavesdropping \u2013 Invading privacy is forbidden.\n43 - Backbiting and slander \u2013 Talking ill of others in their absence is sinful.\n44 - Cursing others \u2013 Habitual cursing invites Allah\u2019s wrath.\n45 - Breaking promises \u2013 Not fulfilling commitments is a sign of hypocrisy.\n46 - Believing in fortune tellers \u2013 Consulting astrologers is disbelief.\n47 - Loving the oppressors \u2013 Supporting tyrants is sinful.\n48 - Being a corrupt leader \u2013 Misguiding people results in grave consequences.\n49 - Indulging in prohibited music \u2013 Certain forms of music can lead to misguidance.\n50 - Engaging in false witness \u2013 Lying in testimony is a major sin.": "2026-10-06T06:05:04.942227",
  "Forgiveness from major sin\nBe sincere \u2014 feel remorse\nPromise not to again\nAsk for forgiveness\nGeneral repentance will work\nQuran:\n\u201cIf you avoid the major sins which you are forbidden.\nWe will remove from your lesser sins and admit you to a noble entrance into paradise\u201d": "2026-10-06T06:05:04.942227",
  "Being tested is an honour\nAllah only tests the ones He loves": "2026-10-06T06:05:04.942227",
  "Allah says\n\u201cIf you avoid the major sins which you are forbidden.\nWe will remove from your lesser sins and admit you to a noble entrance into paradise\u201d\nMajor Sins:\n11 - Committing sodomy \u2013 Homosexual acts are forbidden in Islam.\n12 - Taking or paying interest (Riba) \u2013 Usury is strictly prohibited and leads to destruction.\n13 - Devouring orphan\u2019s wealth \u2013 Wrongfully consuming orphan\u2019s wealth is like eating fire.\n14 - Lying about Allah and His Messenger \u2013 Fabricating lies about religion leads to punishment.\n15 - Fleeing from the battlefield \u2013 Running away from battle without valid reason is sinful.\n16 - Being an unjust ruler \u2013 Oppression by leaders results in severe consequences.\n17 - Pride and arrogance \u2013 Arrogance leads to downfall and rejection from Paradise.\n18 - Ungratefulness \u2013 Not recognizing Allah\u2019s blessings is condemned.\n19 - Intoxicants (alcohol and drugs) \u2013 Consuming intoxicants is the work of Satan.\n20 - Gambling \u2013 Wasting wealth through betting is a sinful act.": "2026-10-07T05:40:40.156510",
