  "My 5 daily namaz cleans my sins\nHadith: Example of a river next to house that I bathe in 5 times a day, making me clean\n\"If there was a river at the door of anyone of you and he took a bath in it five times a day would you notice any dirt on him?\nThey said, \"Not a trace of dirt would be left.\"\nThe Prophet (\ufdfa) added, \"That is the example of the five prayers with which Allah clears evil deeds(minor ofc).": "2026-10-07T05:40:40.156510",
  "Knowing Allah, your Rab is the key to everything(know all names with meanings of Him) - Key to Khushu in namaz\n11 Al-Khaaliq        The Creator, The Maker\n12 Al-Baari\u2019         The Originator\n13 Al-Musawwir       The Fashioner\n14 Al-Ghaffaar       The All- and Oft-Forgiving\n15 Al-Qahhaar        The Subduer, The Ever-Dominating\n16 Al-Wahhaab        The Giver of Gifts\n17 Ar-Razzaaq        The Provider\n18 Al-Fattah         The Opener, The Judge\n19 Al-\u2018Aleem         The All-Knowing, The Omniscient\n20 Al-Qaabid         The Withholder": "2026-10-07T05:40:40.156510",
  "On qiyamat; if prayer is good \u2014 I am saved.\n\"Indeed the first deed by which a servant will be called to account on the Day of Resurrection is his Salat.\nIf it is complete, he is successful and saved.\nBut if it is defective, he has failed and lost.\nIf deficient in farz namaz:\nAllah says: 'Look! Are there any voluntary (prayers) for my worshipper?'\nSo with them, what was deficient in his obligatory (prayers) will be completed.\nThen the rest of his deeds will be treated like that.\u201d": "2026-10-07T05:40:40.156510",
